      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the man in the blue jacket",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the man in the blue jacket (man_in_blue_jacket) as the embodiment of 'freedom of speech'. The meme's structure and text overlay ('freedom of speech' below him) create an implicit identification where the viewer is invited to see themselves as the man, or to identify with his ironic or performative stance on the concept. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but is implied through the meme's format and the viewer's role in interpreting the juxtaposition as a commentary on free speech.",
